  "result": "I changed `notify()` in `src/server/services/notification-service.ts` so it no longer notifies the person who caused the event. I haven't run the test suite; there is an existing test for this case, \"does not notify the actor about their own action\", in `tests/services/notification-service.test.ts`.\n\nThe bug was that the loop over recipients never checked who acted. On `comment.created`, the issue's author and assignee are all notified, even when one of them wrote the comment. The fix skips any recipient whose id matches `payload.actorId`.\n\nBecause the check is inside the shared `notify()`, the same rule now applies to every event type, including mentions (tagging yourself no longer notifies you).",
